      "prompt": "subject_definitions:\n<Video 1> is a surface-orientation motion guide at 24 fps. It supplies the moving subject's body geometry, poses, gestures, head direction and timing.\n<Video 2> is the first frame of the target shot, held still. It supplies the character, outfit, background, materials, colors and lighting.\n\nsummary:\n[keyframe completion + reference generation] Begin from <Video 2> and animate its character with the frame-by-frame poses and motion of <Video 1>. Keep the identity, clothing and environment of <Video 2> throughout.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Video 1> (frame-by-frame subject pose, motion and framing): attribute_transfer - follow the subject's body position, size, gestures and head direction; the picture shows only the character of <Video 2> in natural color.\n<Video 2> (first frame): fully_preserved - preserve its character, outfit, background, colors, materials and lighting as the character moves.\n\ndetailed_description:\n[Shot 1] The shot begins from <Video 2>. The same character performs the changing poses, hand gestures and head movements from <Video 1>, through the final frame, moving into each new pose as it comes. Match the reference performance's timing, framing and camera motion. Keep the character's face, hair and complete outfit of <Video 2> consistent, with coherent arms, hands and fingers. Keep the setting, natural colors and lighting of <Video 2>, including natural contact shadows, in one clean full-frame picture.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nN/A\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A",
